 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 366019,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<p>Build a simple database and create a query that joins information. You are currently working with information about the sales and marketing team. You want to keep track of the team members and the regions they work with. Set up a database with the following tables (remember, you would separate this data into at least two tables to make the database more efficient and easy to work with):</p>\n<b><u>Table:TeamMember</u></b><br>\nTMID<br>\nTMFirstName<br>\nTMLastName<br>\nTMPhone<br>\nTMEmail<br>\n<b><u>Table:SalesRegion</u></b><br>\nSalesRegionName<br>\nSalesRegionNotes<br>\n<b><u>Table:SalesRecord</u></b><br>\nTMID<br>\nSalesRegion\n<p>Once you have set up the tables, create a query that returns the team member’s first and last names and the sales region they are assigned to. Add any fields you think are necessary to create a list of team members’ names with their region. You may want to try sorting to improve the query output.</p>",
